window.CET6_DATA("data/articles/day-105.json",{"day":105,"title":"The Café That Refused to Waste Its Ingredients","targetWords":[{"word":"bitter","gloss":"苦的","context":"Grape skins gave color to a sauce, while honey softened a bitter note.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"butter","gloss":"黄油","context":"A little bacon could season a large pan of vegetables, and cheese offered richness without requiring large amounts of butter.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"pie","gloss":"馅饼","context":"The kitchen could bake a pie or cake, but it did not assume that more sugar always improved dessert.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"cake","gloss":"蛋糕","context":"The kitchen could bake a pie or cake, but it did not assume that more sugar always improved dessert.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"tea","gloss":"茶","context":"One day offered a sandwich and tea, with toast available for a lighter appetite; another offered a hamburger with salad instead of a large fried side.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"dairy","gloss":"乳制品","context":"For a customer avoiding dairy, the kitchen explained alternatives rather than making assumptions.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"orange","gloss":"橙子","context":"An orange supplied juice, a lemon added acidity, and a peach from a neighboring farm could replace a pear when available.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"chocolate","gloss":"巧克力","context":"A small piece of chocolate or a single biscuit sometimes satisfied customers better than an oversized portion.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"juice","gloss":"果汁","context":"An orange supplied juice, a lemon added acidity, and a peach from a neighboring farm could replace a pear when available.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"delicious","gloss":"美味的","context":"A delicious meal did not have to begin with flawless produce.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"pear","gloss":"梨","context":"Both kitchens threw away food that was still safe but no longer attractive: a soft pear, a bruised banana, or a tomato too irregular for a perfect salad.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"tomato","gloss":"西红柿","context":"Both kitchens threw away food that was still safe but no longer attractive: a soft pear, a bruised banana, or a tomato too irregular for a perfect salad.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"turkey","gloss":"火鸡","context":"Leftover turkey or other poultry became soup when stored and reheated safely.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"cafe","gloss":"咖啡馆","context":"When a small cafe opened beside a college cafeteria, its owner expected competition over price.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"nut","gloss":"坚果","context":"A nut mixture provided texture, and a small bowl of soup completed a modest supper.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"cheese","gloss":"奶酪","context":"A little bacon could season a large pan of vegetables, and cheese offered richness without requiring large amounts of butter.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"poultry","gloss":"禽肉","context":"Leftover turkey or other poultry became soup when stored and reheated safely.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"recipe","gloss":"食谱","context":"The owner designed a recipe book around flexibility rather than fixed presentation.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"boil","gloss":"煮","context":"The cooks learned to boil a bean until tender, roast a carrot for deeper flavor, and turn a cucumber into a crisp accompaniment.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"gum","gloss":"口香糖","context":"A customer chewing gum could relax outside, but smoking a cigar was restricted to protect others.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"beverage","gloss":"饮料","context":"Staff described each beverage clearly, including options without alcohol.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"hamburger","gloss":"汉堡包","context":"One day offered a sandwich and tea, with toast available for a lighter appetite; another offered a hamburger with salad instead of a large fried side.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"pub","gloss":"酒馆","context":"The owner declined a suggestion to imitate a pub by selling more liquor, although champagne occasionally accompanied a booked celebration.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"banana","gloss":"香蕉","context":"Both kitchens threw away food that was still safe but no longer attractive: a soft pear, a bruised banana, or a tomato too irregular for a perfect salad.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"lemon","gloss":"柠檬","context":"An orange supplied juice, a lemon added acidity, and a peach from a neighboring farm could replace a pear when available.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"salad","gloss":"色拉","context":"Both kitchens threw away food that was still safe but no longer attractive: a soft pear, a bruised banana, or a tomato too irregular for a perfect salad.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"flavor","gloss":"味道","context":"It required knowledge of flavor, careful storage, and the ability to distinguish a cosmetic defect from a genuine risk to health.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"honey","gloss":"蜂蜜","context":"Grape skins gave color to a sauce, while honey softened a bitter note.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"bacon","gloss":"培根","context":"A little bacon could season a large pan of vegetables, and cheese offered richness without requiring large amounts of butter.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"cafeteria","gloss":"自助餐厅","context":"When a small cafe opened beside a college cafeteria, its owner expected competition over price.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"cucumber","gloss":"黄瓜","context":"The cooks learned to boil a bean until tender, roast a carrot for deeper flavor, and turn a cucumber into a crisp accompaniment.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"dessert","gloss":"甜点","context":"The kitchen could bake a pie or cake, but it did not assume that more sugar always improved dessert.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"grape","gloss":"葡萄","context":"Grape skins gave color to a sauce, while honey softened a bitter note.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"bean","gloss":"豆","context":"The cooks learned to boil a bean until tender, roast a carrot for deeper flavor, and turn a cucumber into a crisp accompaniment.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"bake","gloss":"烤","context":"The kitchen could bake a pie or cake, but it did not assume that more sugar always improved dessert.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"candy","gloss":"糖果","context":"Candy remained an occasional pleasure, not a way to hide every other ingredient.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"carbohydrate","gloss":"碳水化合物","context":"Bread, flour, and other sources of carbohydrate were neither enemies nor automatic solutions.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"carrot","gloss":"胡萝卜","context":"The cooks learned to boil a bean until tender, roast a carrot for deeper flavor, and turn a cucumber into a crisp accompaniment.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"soup","gloss":"汤","context":"Leftover turkey or other poultry became soup when stored and reheated safely.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"toast","gloss":"吐司","context":"One day offered a sandwich and tea, with toast available for a lighter appetite; another offered a hamburger with salad instead of a large fried side.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"biscuit","gloss":"饼干","context":"A small piece of chocolate or a single biscuit sometimes satisfied customers better than an oversized portion.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"champagne","gloss":"香槟酒","context":"The owner declined a suggestion to imitate a pub by selling more liquor, although champagne occasionally accompanied a booked celebration.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"cigar","gloss":"雪茄烟","context":"A customer chewing gum could relax outside, but smoking a cigar was restricted to protect others.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"flour","gloss":"面粉","context":"Bread, flour, and other sources of carbohydrate were neither enemies nor automatic solutions.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"liquor","gloss":"烈酒","context":"The owner declined a suggestion to imitate a pub by selling more liquor, although champagne occasionally accompanied a booked celebration.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"roast","gloss":"烘烤","context":"The cooks learned to boil a bean until tender, roast a carrot for deeper flavor, and turn a cucumber into a crisp accompaniment.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"sandwich","gloss":"三明治","context":"One day offered a sandwich and tea, with toast available for a lighter appetite; another offered a hamburger with salad instead of a large fried side.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"sauce","gloss":"酱汁","context":"Grape skins gave color to a sauce, while honey softened a bitter note.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"supper","gloss":"晚餐","context":"A nut mixture provided texture, and a small bowl of soup completed a modest supper.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"crisp","gloss":"爽脆的","context":"The cooks learned to boil a bean until tender, roast a carrot for deeper flavor, and turn a cucumber into a crisp accompaniment.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null}],"paragraphs":[{"en":"When a small cafe opened beside a college cafeteria, its owner expected competition over price. Instead, she found an opportunity to cooperate. Both kitchens threw away food that was still safe but no longer attractive: a soft pear, a bruised banana, or a tomato too irregular for a perfect salad. The owner designed a recipe book around flexibility rather than fixed presentation. A delicious meal did not have to begin with flawless produce. It required knowledge of flavor, careful storage, and the ability to distinguish a cosmetic defect from a genuine risk to health.","zh":"小咖啡馆在大学食堂旁开业时，店主以为会面对价格竞争，却发现合作机会。两间厨房都丢弃仍安全但外观不佳的食物：变软的梨、碰伤的香蕉，或形状不规则、不适合完美沙拉的番茄。店主围绕灵活使用而非固定外观编写食谱。美味餐食不必始于毫无瑕疵的农产品，而需要了解味道、妥善储存，并能区分外观缺陷与真正的健康风险。"},{"en":"The first experiments used fruit. An orange supplied juice, a lemon added acidity, and a peach from a neighboring farm could replace a pear when available. Grape skins gave color to a sauce, while honey softened a bitter note. The kitchen could bake a pie or cake, but it did not assume that more sugar always improved dessert. A small piece of chocolate or a single biscuit sometimes satisfied customers better than an oversized portion. Candy remained an occasional pleasure, not a way to hide every other ingredient. The aim was to use what arrived without losing the character of the dish.","zh":"最初实验使用水果。橙子提供果汁，柠檬增加酸味，附近农场的桃子上市时可以替代梨。葡萄皮给酱汁上色，蜂蜜柔化苦味。厨房可以烤派和蛋糕，但并不认为糖越多甜点越好。小块巧克力或一块饼干有时比超大份更令顾客满意。糖果仍是偶尔享用的乐趣，而不是遮盖所有其他食材的方式。目标是利用送来的东西，同时保留菜肴特色。"},{"en":"Savory dishes demanded different skills. The cooks learned to boil a bean until tender, roast a carrot for deeper flavor, and turn a cucumber into a crisp accompaniment. Leftover turkey or other poultry became soup when stored and reheated safely. A little bacon could season a large pan of vegetables, and cheese offered richness without requiring large amounts of butter. For a customer avoiding dairy, the kitchen explained alternatives rather than making assumptions. Bread, flour, and other sources of carbohydrate were neither enemies nor automatic solutions. Their value depended on how they fitted into a complete meal.","zh":"咸味菜肴需要不同技巧。厨师学会把豆煮软、烘烤胡萝卜以增强味道，以及把黄瓜做成爽脆配菜。剩火鸡或其他禽肉在安全储存与加热后可以做汤。一点培根能给一大锅蔬菜调味，奶酪无需大量黄油也能带来浓厚口感。遇到不吃乳制品的顾客，厨房解释替代选择，而不擅自假设。面包、面粉与其他碳水化合物来源既非敌人，也非自动解决方案，其价值取决于如何组成完整餐食。"},{"en":"The menu changed with the deliveries. One day offered a sandwich and tea, with toast available for a lighter appetite; another offered a hamburger with salad instead of a large fried side. A nut mixture provided texture, and a small bowl of soup completed a modest supper. Staff described each beverage clearly, including options without alcohol. The owner declined a suggestion to imitate a pub by selling more liquor, although champagne occasionally accompanied a booked celebration. A customer chewing gum could relax outside, but smoking a cigar was restricted to protect others. Hospitality meant making people welcome while also setting reasonable boundaries for a shared space.","zh":"菜单随送货内容改变。有一天供应三明治和茶，也为胃口较小的人准备吐司；另一天供应汉堡配沙拉，而非大份油炸配菜。混合坚果增加口感，小碗汤补全简单晚餐。员工清楚介绍每种饮料，包括无酒精选项。有人建议像酒馆一样多卖烈酒，店主拒绝了，不过预约庆祝活动偶尔会供应香槟。嚼口香糖的顾客可以在外面放松，但抽雪茄受到限制，以保护他人。待客之道意味着让人感到受欢迎，也为共享空间设合理边界。"},{"en":"After a year, the partnership had reduced waste without pretending that every leftover could be saved. Staff kept records, rejected unsafe supplies, and changed plans when quantities were uncertain. Customers learned why an item disappeared from the menu instead of expecting unlimited choice at all times. The cafe became a lesson in practical sustainability: flexibility worked only when supported by reliable standards. Good intentions could not replace hygiene, accounts, or honest communication. Yet when those foundations were secure, a kitchen could turn imperfect ingredients into enjoyable meals and make responsible consumption feel like a normal part of daily life.","zh":"一年后，合作减少浪费，但没有假装每份剩食都能挽救。员工留记录、拒绝不安全供应，并在数量不确定时调整计划。顾客理解菜单项目为什么暂时消失，而不期待任何时候都有无限选择。咖啡馆成为实用可持续性的案例：灵活性只有在可靠标准支持下才有效。好意不能替代卫生、账目或诚实沟通。但这些基础牢固后，厨房就能把外观不完美的食材变成可口饭菜，让负责任的消费成为日常生活的正常部分。"}],"previous":104,"next":106});
